  "novel_mechanics_found": "L6 is a multi-screen transport puzzle built on the same peg-jump mechanic as L5, but introduces a color-8 quad BLOCK that is itself selectable/movable via a jump move -- it can jump OVER a peg without removing it (a movable, indestructible obstacle, not a hazard). A double-socket carrier moves the surviving peg and the block together through a rail network; after seven eastward rail moves the carrier reveals a second chamber containing another peg, two fixed torches, and a rectangular rail loop -- L6 is NOT single-screen like L5, it hides a second chamber behind carrier transport. Winning line: use the block to bridge a narrow wall, remove the narrow peg, return the survivor through the same carrier, remove the central peg, then route the block to column 26 so the survivor can line up and remove the bottom peg.",
  "narrative": "Replayed the banked 312-action L5-verified prefix from a fresh reset (resolver-sourced), confirmed levels_completed=5. Scouted L6: the color-8 block jumps over a peg but does not remove it (movable, indestructible obstacle -- distinct from a peg). The double-socket carrier is not an exit ramp; after seven eastward rail moves it reveals a second hidden chamber with another peg, two fixed torches, and a rectangular rail loop, making L6 a multi-screen puzzle. An early routing attempt sent the block through the left elevator and produced an offscreen disposal/stranded state (dead end); the fix routes the block through the right torch and continues east from the lower junction after the upper-chamber merge. A keyhole click was found to reset only L6 (the 312-step L5-verified prefix stays intact after it fires), which was used to retry the L6 line in-level rather than replaying the full prefix each attempt. The corrected line bridges the narrow wall with the block, removes the narrow peg, returns the survivor through the same carrier, removes the central peg, then routes the block to column 26 so the survivor lines up and removes the bottom peg. levels_completed hit 6 live at session step 615 (of the full 615-action sequence: the 312-action L5-verified prefix plus a 303-action L6 route). A fresh full reproduction gate did not fit in the remaining call budget (would exceed the 700-call session cap), so reproduction_verified is honestly False; the agent spent its remaining ~85 calls scouting L7 rather than stopping at the L6 win. The outer loop independently verified the full 615-action live-observed sequence instead: 5x fresh env.reset() + replay via the registered lf52 GameAdapter, all 5 trials confirmed level=6, state=GameState.NOT_FINISHED (more levels remain beyond 6).",
  "gotchas": [
    "A keyhole click exists that resets ONLY L6 (not the whole game) -- the 312-step L5-verified prefix survives it, making in-level L6 retries cheap relative to replaying the full prefix.",
    "The color-8 quad block jumps over a peg WITHOUT removing it -- confirmed: it is a movable, indestructible obstacle/tool, not a second piece type that participates in removal jumps like pegs do.",
    "The double-socket carrier is NOT an exit from the opening L6 view -- after seven eastward rail moves it reveals a SECOND hidden chamber (another peg, two fixed torches, a rectangular rail loop). Do not assume L6 is single-screen like L5.",
    "Routing the block through the LEFT elevator after the upper-chamber merge leads to an offscreen disposal/stranded dead end; route it through the RIGHT torch and continue east from the lower junction instead.",
    "L7 was reached but not explored before the session budget ran out -- open for next attempt."
